test_hfield -- the hfield command and createpts / poisson_disk with
hfield, NAME (Nov 2026)
=======================================================================

QUICK START

  sh run_hfield_tests.sh [path-to-lagrit]     13 decks, about 5 s
  open summary.html

WHAT IT TESTS

  hfield builds a spacing h from a few sources. For each source i, with
  d the distance to it (0 inside the surface, for inside, surface):

     h_i = H + h_growth * max(0, d - h_band)
     h   = min(h_ceiling, max(h_floor, the smallest h_i))

  hf01 to hf08 evaluate hfields on query vertices (hfield / eval):
  near a point, lines, triangles, a quad; H from an attribute
  (edge_lengths_mean); two sources; inside a cube (quads and
  triangles; and triangles facing in, so inside, against the normals,
  is the outside), a hollow ball (the inner sphere facing into the
  hole), and an L-shaped polygon (vertices only, and lines with one
  turned over). hf09 and hf10: createpts / poisson_disk with a control file
  and with hfield, NAME giving the same h make the same mesh (2D; 3D
  with the octree and with h_lookup, hex_grid). hf11: the ERRORs.
  hf11 also refuses a surface whose triangles do not all face the
  same way. hf12: the WARNING for h_floor below h_spacing_scalar. hf13:
  hfield / dump and hfield / delete.

WHAT IS CHECKED (check_hfield.py)

  LaGriT finished, with no signal or MMVERIFY. The checker computes the
  rule itself (hflib.py), with its own distances (brute force over
  every cell) and inside tests (radius, box, ray crossing), and
  compares h at every vertex to 1e-9. The two poisson meshes of each
  pair must have the same vertices and cells. hf11 to hf13: the texts
  LaGriT must print, and the lattices of hfield / dump.

FILES

  make_hfield.py   writes the decks and the meshes they read (work/)
  check_hfield.py  the checks, the pictures (logs/*.svg), summary.html
  hflib.py         the shapes and the rule, used by both
